<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abulkhair Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1693–1748</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abulkhair Khan was khan of the Junior Juz, the western Kazakh horde, from about 1718. Under pressure from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungars">Dzungars</a> and the Kalmyk Khanate he sought Russian protection, formalised in 1731, the first step in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s absorption of the Kazakh steppe. Russia built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orenburg">Orenburg</a> on his frontier in 1743, and he was killed in 1748 in a feud with a sultan of the Middle Juz.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abulkhair-khan.jpg" alt="Abulkhair Khan" width="320" height="414" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Castle · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abulkhair_Khan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
